    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Taylor Ward** (71.46) anchor our lineup, benefiting significantly from favorable park factors and high-leverage spots in their respective orders. **Lawrence Butler** draws an ideal matchup against Sugano; his elite placement at the top of the order, paired with a solid 4.93 xERA from the opposition, elevates his ceiling significantly. Similarly, **Taylor Ward** benefits from a strong hitting environment and a wind-out advantage at the park, overcoming a slight platoon drag to remain a top-tier start. **Jonathan Aranda** also projects as a core contributor today (70.47) due to his spot in the two-hole and an advantageous matchup against Rodriguez, whose 4.74 xERA suggests plenty of run-scoring potential.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Drew Gilbert**, who fell just short of our 40.0 efficiency floor with a score of 38.69. While **Drew Gilbert** has shown flashes, the combination of a poor lineup spot (#9) and a stagnant platoon matchup against Rolison suppressed his upside, leaving him on the bench in favor of more efficient daily output. We are also keeping a close eye on **Jung Hoo Lee** (44.71); while he is currently in the lineup, his low score due to the platoon disadvantage against Rolison makes him the most volatile asset on the field today. With **Cal Raleigh** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** still shelved on the IL, we are managing a thinned roster, but the aggressive deployment of **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Tyler Freeman**\u2014both of whom cleared the 60-point threshold comfortably\u2014provides necessary stability to our middle infield production.",
